<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-10-1" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Logarithmic Functions</title>

<assemblage component="instructor"><p>In this Lesson we provide only a very light introduction to inverse functions, just enough to support the idea of a log function. Note that we do not use the notation <m>f^{-1}(x)</m> for inverse functions. </p>

<p>GOALS</p>
<p><ul>
    <li><p>Use a graph of <m>f</m> to find values of its inverse</p></li>
    <li><p>Evaluate logarithmic functions</p></li>
    <li><p>Graph logarithmic functions</p></li>
    <li><p>Solve logarithmic equations</p></li>
</ul></p>
</assemblage>

<activity><title>Inverse Functions</title>

    <aside component="instructor"><p>This Activity can serve as a review of the basic functions.</p></aside>           

<introduction><p>For each of the functions shown below,</p>
<p><ol marker="1.">
  <li><p>Complete the table of values, then make a table of values for the inverse function.</p></li>  
  <li><p>Sketch the inverse on the same graph as the function.</p></li>  
  <li><p>For which of these functions is the inverse also a function?</p></li>
</ol></p></introduction>

